PROMPT

Redraw the attached Thorncrown boss as the same forest siege warlord, but give
him a much more grotesque, eccentric personality. The current version reads
like a solemn, polished hero. Make the face and body language unmistakably
odd, lopsided, and unsettling in a playful dark-fantasy way, while keeping the
same recognizable character and equipment.

Give Thorncrown an exaggerated crooked grin, an uneven jutting jaw, a broad
hooked nose, and mismatched expressive eyes: one narrowed and suspicious, the
other larger with its familiar emerald glow. Use irregular blunt teeth, a
slightly protruding lower lip, and a few small bark-like tusks if they fit the
existing face. Keep the expression readable at gameplay scale. The result
should feel grotesque and memorable, not dignified or conventionally heroic,
but also not like a clown or a horror-gore creature.

Make the posture and costume a little more asymmetrical: a slight hunched
shoulder, uneven leaf-and-bark mantle, twisted thorn-crown branches, and
quirky mismatched armor details. Keep these changes subordinate to the
existing silhouette and pose. Retain the dark green foliage, layered bark,
weathered bronze/gold ornaments, emerald accents, and the same large
branch-and-thorn weapon. Do not add a different weapon, shield, companion,
extra limbs, or new story props.

The character remains an imposing mobile siege boss: tall, sturdy, and
readable against a battlefield, with an intentionally grotesque face rather
than a heroic portrait. Keep the eyes, grin, crown, weapon, feet, and full
silhouette clear when the sprite is scaled down. Avoid excessive tiny surface
detail that disappears in-game.

